#SYS/INFOS:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
|docker version  -->	#Shows the current installed version of Docker.                                      |
|docker info    	--> #Displays system-wide information (number of containers, images, storage driver).    |
|docker events   -->	#Streams real-time events from the server (useful for debugging system-level issues).|
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

#DOCKER-COMPOSE:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
|docker-compose up	    --> #Builds, (re)creates, starts, and attaches to containers.                        |
|docker-compose up -d	--> #Starts the containers in the background (detached mode).                        |
|docker-compose build	--> #Builds or rebuilds services (forces a re-read of Dockerfiles).                  |
|docker-compose down	    --> #Stops containers and removes containers, networks, and images created by up.|
|docker-compose down -v	--> #Stops everything and deletes all attached volumes (destroys data).              |
|docker-compose ps	    --> #Lists all containers specifically managed by the current compose file.          |
|docker-compose logs -f	--> #Follows the combined log output of every service in the compose file.           |
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

#CONTAINER-LIFECYCLE:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
|docker ps	                --> #Lists all currently running containers.                                     |
|docker ps -a	            --> #Lists all containers (both running and stopped).                            |
|docker start <container>	--> #Starts one or more stopped containers.                                      |
|docker stop <container>	    --> #Gracefully stops a running container.                                   |
|docker restart <container>	--> #Stops and then immediately starts a container.                              |
|docker kill <container>	    --> #Force-kills a container immediately (no graceful shutdown).             |
|docker rm <container>	    --> #Deletes a stopped container.                                                |
|docker rm -f <container>	--> #Force-deletes a running container.                                          |
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
